  "researcher_notes": "NEW ROW. Distinct from P5984 Rasht-Chelavend Gas Pipeline (operating, 150 km, 42 in, 5.5 bcm/y): this is the onward second-line leg from the Chelvand station near Astara (Gilan) to the Ardabil pressure-boost station (Ardabil province). Re-checked GEM roster (42 existing Iran-gas rows in discovery_context) — no Ardabil/Ardebil row exists; not a rename of P5984. Add-threshold met: (a) sponsor = National Iranian Gas Co / executed by Iran Gas Engineering and Development Co (IGEDC, NIGC subsidiary); (b) endpoints Chelvand(Astara)->Ardabil; (c) concrete step = construction underway (executive operations commenced 30 Shahrivar 1402 = 21 Sep 2023; tie-in to national network completed in 16 hrs, Aug 2024; ~65% progress per Mehr; Dec 2025 Oil Ministry target lists commissioning of 'more than 50 km of Chelvand-Ardabil' by late Mar 2026). Status set to 'construction' (latest concrete evidence, Dec 2025, still pre-commissioning; not yet operating). Specs consistent across sources: 55 km, 30 in, 15.25 MMcm/d design capacity (=5.57 bcm/y; combined with existing line raises Ardabil input to ~30 MMcm/d). Confidence: HIGH — >=2 independent Iranian outlets (SHANA=Oil Ministry news, eghtesademoaser economic outlet, plus Tehran Times English daily and Mehr) agree on route/length/diameter/capacity/status; not a single reprinted wire. NOTE: some English auto-translations render Chelvand as 'Chalus' (Chalus is a different Caspian city) — source Persian is چلوند = Chelvand/Chelavand; OtherEnglishNames carries romanization variants. ROUTE: no public official GIS; corridor is the ~55 km Astara/Chelvand -> Ardabil city route through mountainous/forested Gilan-Ardabil terrain; endpoints known, geometry not mapped (route left for routes-repo; not fabricated). Owner 'National Iranian Gas Co' reuses existing GEM entity (entity_lookup: 100 match) — no new entity created. Capacity converted 15.25 MMcm/d x 365 = 5.57 bcm/y to match tracker CapacityUnits='bcm/y'."
